# 7.1.acuity.envelope.emergency.stone

## .what

set the **emergency floor** — which live scenarios demand care *now*, and what the worst-case bound
of the superposition forces as the minimum urgency. acuity is set by the **envelope**: the most
time-critical live scenario sets the floor, even if it is not the most probable.

## .inputs

- `5.3.scenario.rerank.redteam.refine.yield.md` — the live survivor set + ranks
- `6.1.scenario.superposition.bounds.yield.md` — the worst-case bounds

## .do

- scan every live scenario for a worst-case bound that is **time-critical** (deteriorates in hours,
  or a window to intervene closes)
- if any un-eliminated scenario is time-critical, the acuity floor is **emergency** — state it
  plainly, name the scenario that forces it
- write the **red-line signs** — the concrete observations that mean "go now", drawn from the
  worst-case bounds

## .emit

into `7.1.acuity.envelope.emergency.yield.md` — the emergency floor (set or not), the scenario that
forces it, and the red-line go-now signs.

## .done when

the emergency floor is stated, the scenario that sets it is named, and the red-line signs are listed.
